---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import KeybindingTable from '../../components/KeybindingTable.astro';
---

<Docs title="CLI Reference" description="Complete command-line reference for grüt — flags, commands, environment variables, and usage examples.">
  <h1>CLI Reference</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    All commands, flags, and environment variables for the <code>grut</code>
    command-line interface.
  </p>

  <h2>Root Command</h2>
  <pre><code>grut [flags] [command]</code></pre>
  <p>
    AI-native terminal file explorer, git client, and agent orchestrator.
    Running <code>grut</code> with no arguments launches the interactive TUI
    in the current directory.
  </p>

  <h2>Global Flags</h2>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: '--no-ai', action: 'Disable AI features for this operation' },
    { key: '--demo', action: 'Launch with a demo project to explore grüt' },
    { key: '--layout <name>', action: 'Start with a layout: explorer, git, review, agent, or full' },
    { key: '--reset-welcome', action: 'Reset first-run state so the welcome screen shows on next launch' },
    { key: '-h, --help', action: 'Show help information' },
    { key: '-v, --version', action: 'Show version information' },
  ]} />

  <h2>Environment Variables</h2>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'GRUT_LOG', action: 'Path to a log file (enables debug logging)' },
    { key: 'GRUT_NERD_FONT', action: 'Set to 1 to force Nerd Font icons in any terminal' },
    { key: 'GRUT_FORCE_TERMINAL', action: 'Set to any non-empty value to bypass the MinTTY/MSYS check on Windows' },
  ]} />
  <pre><code># Enable debug logging
export GRUT_LOG=/tmp/grut-debug.log
grut</code></pre>

  <h2>Commands</h2>

  <h3>version</h3>
  <p>Print the current grüt version.</p>
  <pre><code>grut version</code></pre>

  <h3>update</h3>
  <p>
    Update grüt to the latest release. Downloads are SHA-256 verified to
    ensure integrity.
  </p>
  <pre><code>grut update</code></pre>

  <h3>status</h3>
  <p>Print a summary of the working tree status. Add <code>--json</code> for scriptable output.</p>
  <pre><code>grut status
grut status --json</code></pre>

  <h3>config</h3>
  <p>Inspect grüt configuration.</p>
  <pre><code># Validate the active config
grut config check

# Print one resolved value by dotted key
grut config get git.default_branch

# Print the full default config as TOML
grut config defaults</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'check', action: 'Validate the active configuration' },
    { key: 'get <key>', action: 'Print a single resolved config value' },
    { key: 'defaults', action: 'Print the default configuration as TOML' },
  ]} />

  <h3>theme</h3>
  <p>Inspect grüt themes.</p>
  <pre><code># List available themes
grut theme list</code></pre>

  <h3>keys</h3>
  <p>Print keybindings from the command line.</p>
  <pre><code>grut keys
grut keys --filter commit
grut keys --sections
grut keys --json</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: '--filter <text>', action: 'Only show sections, keys, or actions matching the text' },
    { key: '--section <id>', action: 'Only show the section with this id' },
    { key: '--sections', action: 'Print available keybinding section ids and titles' },
    { key: '--json', action: 'Print keybindings as JSON' },
  ]} />

  <h3>clean</h3>
  <p>
    Remove grüt's transient session and diagnostic data. Without
    <code>--force</code> it only previews what would be removed.
  </p>
  <pre><code># Preview what would be removed
grut clean

# Delete the transient data
grut clean --force</code></pre>

  <h3>completion</h3>
  <p>Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell.</p>
  <pre><code>grut completion bash
grut completion zsh
grut completion fish
grut completion powershell</code></pre>

  <h3>report</h3>
  <p>View crash reports and file GitHub issues for them.</p>
  <pre><code># List all crash reports
grut report --list

# Show a specific report by ID
grut report --show &lt;id&gt;

# Open a GitHub issue for the most recent crash
grut report --latest

# Clear all crash reports
grut report --clear</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: '--list', action: 'List all crash reports' },
    { key: '--show <id>', action: 'Show a specific crash report by ID' },
    { key: '--latest', action: 'Open a GitHub issue for the most recent crash' },
    { key: '--clear', action: 'Clear all crash reports' },
    { key: '--no-browser', action: 'Print the issue URL instead of opening the browser' },
    { key: '--json', action: 'Print list output as JSON' },
  ]} />

  <h3>mcp</h3>
  <p>
    Run grüt as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, communicating via
    stdin/stdout JSON-RPC. Use <code>grut mcp tools</code> to list the tools
    the server exposes.
  </p>
  <pre><code># Standard MCP mode (stdin/stdout)
grut mcp

# List the MCP tools grüt exposes
grut mcp tools</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'tools', action: 'List the MCP tools grüt exposes' },
    { key: '--socket <path>', action: 'Serve over a Unix socket (not yet implemented)' },
  ]} />

  <h3>run</h3>
  <p>
    Execute an AI-powered git workflow shortcut. Shortcuts are predefined
    sequences of git operations that can be invoked by name.
  </p>
  <pre><code># Run a shortcut
grut run pr-review

# List available shortcuts
grut run --list

# Describe what a shortcut does
grut run --describe pr-review

# Preview without executing
grut run --dry-run pr-review

# Skip confirmation prompts
grut run --no-confirm pr-review</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: '--list', action: 'List all available shortcuts' },
    { key: '--describe <name>', action: 'Show what a shortcut does without running it' },
    { key: '--dry-run', action: 'Preview the operations without executing them' },
    { key: '--no-confirm', action: 'Skip confirmation prompts' },
  ]} />

  <h3>ext</h3>
  <p>
    Manage grüt extensions. Extensions add new panels, commands, and
    integrations to the TUI.
  </p>
  <pre><code># Create a new extension scaffold
grut ext create my-extension

# Install an extension
grut ext install my-extension

# Remove an extension
grut ext remove my-extension

# List installed extensions
grut ext list

# Enable / disable an extension
grut ext enable my-extension
grut ext disable my-extension

# Show extension details
grut ext info my-extension</code></pre>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'create', action: 'Scaffold a new extension project' },
    { key: 'install', action: 'Install an extension' },
    { key: 'remove', action: 'Remove an installed extension' },
    { key: 'list', action: 'List all installed extensions' },
    { key: 'enable', action: 'Enable a disabled extension' },
    { key: 'disable', action: 'Disable an extension without removing it' },
    { key: 'info', action: 'Show details about an extension' },
  ]} />

  <h2>Examples</h2>
  <pre><code># Launch grüt in the current directory
grut

# Launch with AI features disabled
grut --no-ai

# Try grüt with a demo project
grut --demo

# Update to the latest version
grut update

# Use as an MCP server in your AI toolchain
grut mcp</code></pre>
</Docs>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
